furnished home was in total disarray. Draws had been upended, and Robert's belongings were strewn everywhere. The place had been thoroughly ransacked. In the middle of the chaos was Robert, sprawled on a couch. The white jumpsuit he was wearing was covered in blood. He had been stabbed five times in the back, once in the chest, and his throat had been slashed. Robert's left ear was also missing. As his friends cast their eyes upwards, the sight before them grew even more shocking. Scrawled on a wall in Robert's own blood were the words, Satan save Zodiac, followed by a crosshair symbol. Despite the message tying the murder to the Zodiac, detectives were quick to rule out any

