00:21:17.000 --> 00:22:18.000
The San Francisco Police Department instructed the Chronicle to run a brief article about the card in order to placate the Zodiac. They were certain this latest note was genuinely from him, due to the bomb threats which had also been made in previous Zodiac letters. 3. The Case Detectives had always been careful to keep those references under wraps out of fear they may cause unnecessary panic. 4. On May 31, law enforcement made the difficult decision to publicize the bomb threat. 5. Suddenly the risk felt too great. 6. It was 5.28 am on June 19, 1970, when the sound of gun shots rang out over Waller Street in San Francisco's Lower Haight neighborhood. There were three shots in total, fired in quick

